    // next_state is determined based on current state and input 'in'

    // For each state, determine next_state for in=0 and in=1
    // Using one-hot encoding, only one bit is 1 at a time

    // A (0001) -> A (0001) when in=0, B (0010) when in=1
    // B (0010) -> C (0100) when in=0, B (0010) when in=1
    // C (0100) -> A (0001) when in=0, D (1000) when in=1
    // D (1000) -> C (0100) when in=0, B (0010) when in=1

